s this sort of chance that your  squad you're just four or five guys  could go and take an objective on the  other side of the map or go and sort of  harass an objective on the other side of  the map while the main team was taking  over like a position centrally located  this with its roots and different ways  to sort of sneak around really does  bring back the opportunity for that kind  of gameplay I think also you know with  the size of the map and the type of  gameplay you're talking about all the  enough World War three also gets the RPG  tank balanced today that battlefield has  been kind of getting away from like I  remember in the battlefield alpha and  beta  if you've lucked into a tank you could  oftentimes get destroyed by an engineer  before you even knew that they were  there the RPG tank fights in this are  better because they typically take place  at longer ranges they're more  cat-and-mouse it takes three or four  hits and sometimes you run out of ammo  before you can kill it tanks can also go  to the back of the map and heal up so it  feels like the older balanced versus I  don't know like everything you so sped  up these days and in battlefield in a  way that I just don't find to be  compelling anymore one of the things I  like about this game so far is the  weapon customization and loadout options  it's similar to insurgency in that it's  based on weight and at least at this  point in the in the early access  everything is available to you so you  don't have to unlock things you can just  go in there and modify the weapons the  way you want them plug them in to your  loadout and it'll just be dependent on  how encumber do you want to be and that  really gives you a lot of freedom to  decide how you want to play the game and  what kind of sort of tactical player you  want to be rather than being dependent  on unlocks the way battlefield has  become so tedious with unlocking I  really like these games that are sort of  treating you more like an adult on that  level you're treated like you can figure  out what you want and you're gonna have  those toys available to you right away  so I don't want to make this all sound  too cheery because World War 3 does have  some aspects that it definitely lags  behind battlefield on it cannot touch  frostbite when it comes to destruction  sound design I would say is bad I agree  with that the sound design needs  significant improvement I know it's  early access but if they're gonna pour a  resource into something I would put in a  sound because we saw how effective sound  is in insurgency  a game that has probably has the best  sound that I've heard in a long time and  it makes a huge difference in how you  perceive that game it absolutely does  like the you know the graphics are  probably a little bit better in World  War 3 but insurgency the sound really  transports you to the environment and  the sound is definitely lacking in World  War 3  there's also issues that they're gonna  have to work out with spawn killing or  bad spawn placements battlefields come a  long way on their danger spawn system  and trying may be successful sometimes  not others to get you spawning in places  where you don't instantly die even if  they're not doing it perfectly there you  can tell that they care about it you  know the dangerous planning thing was  actually one of the best decisions they  made in a long time in that game then  there's just your average bugs from an  early access title like tanks flying off  into the sky when you get into them  falling through the map you know the  usual stuff you'll find from a game  that's early on I agree that it's  important to keep this in the context of  early access it's a little bit buggy it  takes a while to get into a match I was  finding that when I would create a  custom loadout it wouldn't save between  sessions of the game so there's there's  definitely these things that show that  it is not completely polished and has a  ways to go it's currently $28 for an  early access title and they're gonna  start adding Maps as they go  battlefields full price we don't really  know fully what's gonna be there at  launch this roadmap I think was supposed  to be a good thing but I kind of read it  as in most of the game I was expecting  to be there won't be there at launch and  look we could be wrong  we've played an alpha and a beta and  I've also played through three of the  war stories or at least portions of  three war stories so I honestly can't  say that after all that I feel like I  have a good grasp of what exactly  battlefields gonna feel like at launch  but right now the way it's been marketed  and from what I've seen it feels more  like an early access title I know that  might sound a little harsh and will of  course give it a fair shake but at the  end of the day world war 3 has a shot of  peeling off people who want a modern  shooter who miss battlefield 3 and 4 who  aren't super into the world war 2  setting for either mechanical or other  reasons and who want to stick with a  game that's being developed Ryan do you  think World War 3 has a shot against the  battlefield this year I think it  deserves a shot  like it as you said it is derivative we  are returning to basically trodden  territory but it does sort of feel like  that game if you miss the modern  battlefields it's kind of got that tone  to it you know as soon as you spawn in  and it's raining and it's dark and it's  gloomy it's almost like being back and  you know Grand Bazaar or to run highway  or something like that like it it  captures some of that feeling and I  haven't felt that in a little while in a  battlefield game alright well we'll just  have to see World War 3 is currently out  in early access and battlefield 5 is out  next month so we'll follow up once we  get our hands on battlefield 5 and of  course we'll have a full review for you  on gamespot comm thanks for watching let  us know how you feel about the two games  in the co